{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794694771,"nonce":"zwXrDKmLKYzs7YwGocwKGMh+0No=","title":"Generated hxcpp code does not compile with hxcpp 4.3.2 on Linux GCC","message":"On the NUC (Linux, GCC, haxelib hxcpp 4.3.2, Haxe 4.3.6), `hxn check cpp` and\n`hxn check cppia` in hxn-av fail to compile code hxn generates for every\nlibrary:\n\n    ./src/hxn/Handle.cpp:23:32: error: conversion from 'Dynamic' to 'void*' is ambiguous\n    ./src/hxn/Handle.cpp:11:36: note: initializing argument 1 of 'void hxn::Handle_obj::__construct(void*)'\n\nand for CPPIA, in the library's native class:\n\n    ./src/media/HxnXaviNative.cpp:3862:59: error: conversion from 'Dynamic' to 'void*' is ambiguous\n    ./src/media/HxnXaviNative.cpp:266:48: note: initializing argument 1 of 'static hxn::Handle media::HxnXaviNative_obj::hxnOwn(void*)'\n\nThe same sources compile and pass on macOS with hxcpp from git, and in\nhxn-window's Linux CI, which installs hxcpp from git at 615adc7. So the\ndifference is probably hxcpp 4.3.2, the current haxelib release, rather than\nLinux. A user who runs `haxelib install hxcpp` gets 4.3.2.\n\nTo reproduce: on Linux with `haxelib install hxcpp` (4.3.2), run\n`hxn check cpp` in any hxn library, such as hxn-window or hxn-av.\n\nTo do: confirm 4.3.2 is the cause, then either cast the handle argument so\nthe Dynamic-taking constructor (`__Create`) and the CPPIA wrapper convert\nunambiguously, or state the minimum hxcpp in the docs.","files":null}]}